{"id":"relief","title":"Federal COVID relief paid to providers the City also funds","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"Which City-funded organizations also drew federal COVID relief for health providers, and did the same costs get paid twice?","finding":"25 organizations the City pays appear by name in the federal Provider Relief Fund list for California, with $38.5 million between them; 8 of those also hold a federal paycheck-protection loan under a matching name ($14.9 million). The City paid the 25 a combined $545 million in fiscal 2020 to 2022. San Francisco recipients as a whole received $651 million in 1,318 payments.","how":"Recipient names in the federal list were matched to the names of City-paid nonprofits. Loan amounts come from the federal paycheck-protection file by the same name match. City payments are the ledger totals for fiscal 2020 to 2022.","limits":"Taking relief money is not a warning sign: it was offered to every eligible provider and most of it was paid by formula. The federal list has only a name, a city and an amount, so a match is by name alone and a national body with the same name (listed in another city) may be a different legal entity. The question worth asking is narrow: whether relief money, a forgiven loan and City contract payments were each claimed for the same payroll or the same lost revenue. Only the recipient's own reports to the federal government can answer it. The fiscal year of a City payment here is the Controller's: the year its files put the payment under, the same year the organization pages show. For a small part of the money the voucher was issued in an earlier fiscal year than that: $97.3 million of the $10.22 billion in the City's nonprofit spending file for the nonprofits profiled here, going by the matching lines of the payment file; for a further $152.7 million the payment file has no matching lines, or lines that mix payments and reversals, so it cannot be said.","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Organization","type":"org"}